- op: discuss  # 4bfe
  at: '2026-09-06T11:27:04Z'  # 4bfe
  by: agent  # 4bfe
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4bfe
  clock: 4  # 4bfe
  nonce: 4bfe  # 4bfe
  message: "DONE 2026-09-06 (PR #791). Design (1) and (2) shipped as filed; (3) measured.\n\nSHIPPED. c.yaml: sys/socket send/sendto/sendmsg dual net_send + ipc_send, recv/recvfrom/recvmsg dual net_recv + ipc_recv, boundary_ruling call_site_undecidable, abstains_to net_* (today's answer); connect stays single-rowed; the stale unistd.write ipc_send note rewritten (write(STDOUT_FILENO) is `logging` under WI-dutah). c.py: _c_socket_target_kind stamps io_target_kind from the descriptor argument -- inline socket(FAMILY, ..); sv[0]/sv[1] after a preceding socketpair(.., sv) (a new hop: socketpair binds an array by argument, so the last-binding helper cannot see it); a bare identifier through _c_binding_rhs; one accept/accept4 hop to the listener's family. AF_UNIX/AF_LOCAL/PF_* -> pipe; AF_INET/AF_INET6/PF_* -> net_stream; PF_NETLINK, PF_PACKET, AF_VSOCK, a variable family, a parameter, a struct field -> nothing (INV-zumin: one answer or none). 31 analyzer tests (test_c_socket_fd_origin.py) + 7 catalogue tests (test_target_kind_fallback_entries.py::TestTheCSocketFamilyRows).\n\nMEASURED (3), arm A on dev ef54494949, arm B on the branch, twelve C repositories, 324 sites, every arm cold; instrument ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/baran_sockets_09062026/ (README, ab_compare.out):\n  stamped 27 (pipe 19, net_stream 8); MOVED 3, all recvmsg net_recv -> ipc_recv on `pipe`; REMOVED 0.\n  haproxy src/sock.c:554, :585   sock = socket(PF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0) at 518, no rebinding   -- correct (fd-passing over the master CLI unix socket)\n  passt   passt-repair.c:199     if ((s = socket(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0)) < 0) at 104        -- correct\n  Nothing moved in conmon, dbus-broker, firejail, fluent-bit, guacamole-server, gvisor, libvfio-user, tmate, tmux, torsocks.\nThe 16 `pipe` stamps on bare send/recv and the 8 net_stream stamps moved nothing: bare send/recv never classify (below), and net_stream keeps the net_* row.\n\nTHE ITEM'S OWN INSTANCE DID NOT MOVE, as the premise entry above predicted: tmux's sendmsg/recvmsg take the descriptor as a parameter (compat/imsg-buffer.c); the socket() calls are two functions away. That needs WI-famig's cross-function summaries (entry left there) or a repository-level \"no AF_INET socket anywhere\" inference, which is the 0012 adjudicator's move and a loosening in the false-all-clear direction -- not built. 0012's tmux deduction therefore stands as a deduction; this PR removes the mechanism that produced it wherever the descriptor's origin is visible in the function.\n\nRESIDUALS FILED: WI-lajus-mobod-ganom-vozig-rudus-mamih-jabup-gidag (bare send/recv are ambiguous_names with no module slot from #include -- 156 of 324 sites classify as nothing; INV-linub's class in C, Phase 6) and WI-rimon-tajan-ruraz-kigun-gobal-somuz-napib-vigot (fluent-bit binds 116 sendto/recv sites by name to a vendored nuttx shim -- C name-only resolution's wrong callee). unistd.read/write over a socket descriptor is INV-vaduk's own residual and is pinned out of scope by test_a_write_over_a_socket_is_out_of_scope_here."  # 4bfe
